  "published": "2026-10-16T13:32:25.563Z",
  "releaseNotes": "Fixed semi-transparent content (e.g. images with a soft mask or fills with an opacity below 100%) rendering too light, often completely white, when rendering with a white background, a regression introduced in 1.0.0-alpha07: Pdfium returns straight (non-premultiplied) alpha, but it was composited as if premultiplied. Fixed password-protected documents never opening, because the password was marshalled as UTF-16 instead of a byte string. Documents that cannot be loaded now throw PdfiumException with a PdfiumErrorCode (e.g. Password, Format) instead of returning an unusable PdfDocument, rendering a disposed page now throws instead of using a freed handle, and disposal is safe to call concurrently.",
